==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Meow-sketeer''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Like other [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]]-exclusive units, the first and second forms of D'artanyan each play a different role. While his Evolved form possesses high DPS against traited foes, his first form can be quickly stacked to deal decent damage, even more thanks to his massive damage ability. His range is quite low but he makes up for this with his [[Long Distance]] attacks, allowing him to reach up to 360 range and hit past the front clash lines of the battle.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
In his Evolved form, Meow-sketeer now takes the role of a midrange rusher, packing a fast 24 speed and quick attacks. This capitaine of the cat army's shining stat is definitely his damage output, dealing an impressive 13.4K DPS to Traited enemies at Lv.30 (10.1K to traits without fruit treasures). His [[Long Distance]] is not just a little bonus, either. Reaching 550 range, Meow-sketeer can easily demolish backline support enemies in just a few shots, while having great area coverage.

However, Meow-skeeteer is not without a few irritating weaknesses. Firstly, his Long Distance gives him a blindspot of 200. This lets some melee enemies sneak into his blindspot, though his many knockbacks can bring him outside the enemies' range. Also, Meow-sketeer packs a 1.5 second foreswing. While not too long, Meow-sketeer is a rusher operating close to enemy territory, and might mandate the use of support against certain rapid-attacking ranged enemies or aggressive peons. Most glaringly, Meow-sketeer has 45.9K HP at Lv.30, making him frail especially considering he is a rusher. Be sure to protect him well.

If you're lucky enough to obtain Meow-sketeer early on, you're in luck. His monstrous damage output can shred apart most early-game and mid-game content, such as the [[Stories of Legend]]. However, later on, he faces tough competition from a talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. With his Explosion Talent maxed out, Bahamut Cat has over 4 times Meow-sketeer's anti-Traited DPS, with other advantages of speed, faster foreswing and being good against Traitless. After unlocking Awakened Bahamut Cat's Talents, Meow-sketeer is still usable, but must differentiate himself with his range and piercing LD that allows him to snipe enemy backliners.

Overall, D'artanyan is a great pull, as his first form takes the role of a spammable attacker, and his stronger evolved form shines as an extremely dangerous midrange rusher with anti-wave and sniping capabilities. Despite his poor survivability and matchups against traitless, Meow-sketeer still packs a punch in the early-mid game while still seeing use later on due to his pierce.

